{
  "id": 111902057,
  "iid": 3866,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "PFCP: Fix Enterprise IE generic decoding offsets",
  "description": "Reduce by two every offset in generic enterprise IE decoding.\n\nCurrent code generates this behavior:\n\n![image](/uploads/8495d5c82022b0924fac1a07a16ec50e/image.png)\n\nThe group information is OK (it detects and enterprise and the IE code correctly) but inside the IE it has an offset of 2.\n\n\"Enteprise specific IE type\" is pointing to [00 03] when it should point to [80 01].\n\nThe length should be [00 03] but it is [0f ea].\n\nThis patch changes the used offset and generates this output:\n\n![image](/uploads/2019016d4e0ab04b6c6259bcc9f1cfd6/image.png)\n\nNow the information is OK:\n- Enterprise IE Type: [80 01]\n- IE Length [00 03]\n- Enterprise code: [0f ea]\n- Data: [01]\n\nYou can use this test packet:\n```\n0000   00 00 00 00 00 00 FA FA FA FA FA FA 81 00 00 01\n0010   08 00 45 00 00 33 a3 81 00 00 3f 11 07 62 00 00\n0020   00 01 00 00 00 02 22 65 22 65 00 1F 4c 95 23 36\n0030   00 13 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 00 00 01 10 80 01\n0040   00 03 0F EA 01\n```",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-08-11T13:09:21.506Z",
  "updated_at": "2021-08-12T10:14:10.809Z",
